<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">26052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>United States forces struck missile sites and mine-laying boats in southern Iran on the same day Tehran's central bank governor flew to Doha to negotiate the release of frozen assets.</s> <s>Centcom killed four members of the Revolutionary Guard while Qatari mediators bridged the gap that had stalled every prior round.</s> <s>The seven-week ceasefire is being treated not as a pause, but as a leverage instrument... Tehran is being asked to sign while still being struck.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Affiliates of Jamaat-e-Islami have demolished centuries-old Sufi shrines across Bangladesh, dismantling the country's syncretic Islamic tradition in real time.</s> <s>The shrines, known as mazars, lost their state protection when Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina was ousted, and the caretaker administration has not restored security.</s> <s>This is intra-Muslim oppression, where one school of Islamic practice is being violently erased by another inside the same ummah.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Costa Rican investigators say Nicaragua's government paid to assassinate Roberto Samcam, a former Sandinista commander gunned down in San José last June.</s> <s>President Daniel Ortega has now crossed the line from authoritarianism into transnational repression, hiring killers to reach opponents on foreign soil.</s> <s>Extraterritorial assassination is no longer a behaviour of only the top-tier autocracies... it's becoming a tool of mid-sized regimes with criminal-economy revenue streams.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Niger's military government has cancelled every defence agreement with France, severing ties that predated independence and that no elected government had ever touched.</s> <s>Four pacts, terminated at once, end a French military presence in the Sahel that survived sixty years of post-colonial politics.</s> <s>Chad and Senegal still hold their French agreements... but the question now is for how long.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Suspected Ebola deaths in the Democratic Republic of Congo have reached two hundred and twenty, with a cross-border fatality already recorded in Uganda.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> has released only three point nine million dollars from its contingency fund, while five hundred million in pledges sits undisbursed and the Bundibugyo strain still has no vaccine.</s> <s>This is what global health governance looks like when pledges arrive slower than a virus moves down a bus route.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia's foreign minister Sergey Lavrov phoned Marco Rubio to advise Washington to evacuate diplomats and citizens from Kyiv before Moscow begins what he called systematic strikes on Ukrainian decision-making centres.</s> <s>European missions refused to leave, and Kyiv called the warning blackmail, asking Western partners for additional sanctions.</s> <s>A call like this normally precedes either a major air offensive or a deliberate signal that the Kremlin wants the Americans out of the room before talks resume.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Forensic Architecture's satellite analysis shows Israel has built twenty-five kilometres of earth berms inside Gaza, west of the ceasefire line agreed last autumn.</s> <s>The walls push Israeli control past sixty percent of the strip, and thirty-eight military forts are under construction along the eastern edge.</s> <s>What was negotiated as a withdrawal line is being redrawn in compacted soil... and the maps of Gaza are being rewritten faster than the diplomacy that produced them.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India has scrapped its forced gas-surrender mandate after the Hormuz closure cut ninety percent of the country's liquefied petroleum gas supply, the petroleum ministry confirmed.</s> <s>Nearly sixty thousand households had already surrendered their cooking-gas connections in a one-way push toward piped natural gas, only for many to move for work to areas where no pipeline yet reaches.</s> <s>It's the largest household-energy switch under way anywhere on Earth, and the bureaucratic plumbing keeps getting rewritten as the social reality bites.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Australia's Hunter Valley, <sub alias="A G L">AGL</sub> demolished the two hundred-and-seventy-metre chimneys of the Liddell coal-fired power station on Tuesday, ending fifty years of baseload generation.</s> <s>The site will become a five-hundred-megawatt battery — and once a baseload plant is rubble, no political reversal can restore its capacity.</s> <s>The rich-world coal phase-out is now physically irreversible at the asset level, which changes the energy policy any future government can plausibly run.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa's SA Lithium has earmarked one hundred and fifty homes near Port Shepstone for demolition to make way for an open-pit mine.</s> <s>The environmental assessment was filed by the company's own consultant, and South African law required relocation agreements to be settled before mining began... neither happened.</s> <s>Lawyers have demanded the assessment restart from the beginning... but the first forced relocations are already scheduled.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>An independent analysis by Carbon Brief finds that China has retroactively redefined its core carbon-intensity metric, creating an accounting gap of roughly seven hundred million tonnes a year — the size of Germany's entire annual emissions.</s> <s>Under the new metric, Beijing could meet its twenty-thirty Paris pledges without cutting a single additional tonne.</s> <s>International climate accounting is now a forum where definitions move faster than emissions, and the verification regime has no answer when a major power simply redraws its own ruler.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A study of two psychiatric hospitals in Sana'a found that thirty-six percent of inpatients are on antipsychotic combinations known to prolong the cardiac QT interval, a setup that triggers sudden death in well-resourced systems.</s> <s>Only one in four patients had any electrocardiogram monitoring, and Yemen's war-damaged health system cannot supply the rest.</s> <s>The global mental-health treatment gap isn't only about access... it's about prescribing patterns the world's essential-medicines lists do not regulate.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>New modelling from a London research team suggests that the dormancy of the supermassive black hole at the centre of our galaxy, Sagittarius A-star, may be part of what makes Earth habitable.</s> <s>An active galactic core irradiates an entire galaxy, sterilising worlds far beyond its immediate reach.</s> <s>The implication is that the search for life must map galactic neighbourhoods, not only the stars at their centre.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has blocked the prediction market Polymarket, applying an existing gambling statute to crypto-settled contracts and setting a template that other Muslim-majority governments can now cite.</s> <s>The block covers a market of two hundred and eighty million people, and the ministry says similar platforms will follow.</s> <s>A category of finance that was designed to evade national regulation has just met a national regulator that didn't need a new law to act.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At Google's I/O conference, the company made artificial intelligence the default mode of search, ending the link-based index it has maintained since nineteen ninety-eight.</s> <s>A United States court ruled two years ago that the old index was an illegal monopoly... the company has now retired it on its own terms.</s> <s>Paid alternatives like Kagi are gaining users, and the search market is genuinely contestable for the first time in more than two decades.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Southeast Asian governments lack any binding framework against coordinated artificial-intelligence disinformation, even as agents now campaign in Bahasa, Tagalog, Thai, and Vietnamese at near-zero cost.</s> <s>Platform moderation in Indonesia, the region's largest electorate, is the thinnest in the bloc.</s> <s>Existing rules cover human-run influence operations... they were never written for swarms that run themselves.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>